IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ro-orders`

-- Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act gives a right to apply to the person seeking to be protected and puts its duties and its offences on
-- the person bound by an order. So there are two seats:
--   - the person who wants to be protected: the baseline's seat (ro-orders.l4), 22 questions;
--   - the person an order is sought or made against (the respondent, the person bound), 11 questions.
-- The court, the registrar, the authorised magistrate and the police are never seats; what they may or must do appears
-- as what it means for the person asking. A parent, guardian or child welfare officer applying for a child asks the
-- protected person's questions on the child's behalf ("May this person apply for the order to protect me").
--
-- SITUATION (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does
-- not hold, without reading anything else. There is one situation input, shared by both roles with the same name, type
-- and @desc, so the form asks it once: `the order so far` (`The order so far`): no order yet, an interim order, a final
-- order, or a police order. The Act ties these questions to an order having been made:
--   - the 21 days to return the endorsement copy (s 31) and what follows if it is not returned (s 32): an interim order;
--   - how long a final order lasts (ss 16A, 16B, 37, 50A): an interim order (which becomes final, s 32) or a final order;
--   - how long a police order binds, its 24 hours to be served, and that it cannot be renewed (ss 30F, 30H): a police
--     order;
--   - breach, its penalties, repeated breach, the time to prosecute and aiding a breach (ss 61, 61A, 61B): any order.
-- Where the order so far is a police order, the breach questions do not ask which kind of order was made: it is a
-- police order. The protected person's questions about getting an order (the relationship, the violence, which order,
-- who may apply, telephone orders, interim orders, police orders on the spot) arise in every situation, and take none;
-- so does the respondent's question whether any order can be made against them at all.
--
-- The rules are in ro-orders.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the protected person each answer, where
-- its situation holds, is the baseline export's own answer, wrapped. The respondent's questions call the same rules,
-- with two helpers for what the baseline does not export (s 32(2), s 61(6)). No exported question takes a DEONTIC or
-- EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I want to be protected from someone`
    `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me`

-- The situation: whether an order has been made yet, and which.
DECLARE `The order so far` IS ONE OF
    `no order has been made yet`
    `an interim order has been made`
    `a final order has been made`
    `a police order has been made`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    months HAS `how many months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    days HAS `how many days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Hours` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    hours HAS `how many hours` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Which order, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS AN `Order that can protect me`

-- s 61(6): the time to bring a prosecution for a breach.
DECLARE `Time to prosecute` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `within years of the day of the breach` HAS `how many years` IS A NUMBER
    `not set by this Act: s 61(6) does not cover a breach of an MRO`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The situation checks list every value and have no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31: a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE takes the
-- OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing, so a case could not show the value was not read).
GIVEN `the order so far` IS A `The order so far`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no order has been made` IF
    CONSIDER `the order so far`
    WHEN `no order has been made yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an interim order has been made` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final order has been made` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a police order has been made` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the order so far` IS A `The order so far`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no interim order has been made` IF
    CONSIDER `the order so far`
    WHEN `no order has been made yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an interim order has been made` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final order has been made` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police order has been made` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the order so far` IS A `The order so far`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no interim or final order has been made` IF
    CONSIDER `the order so far`
    WHEN `no order has been made yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an interim order has been made` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final order has been made` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a police order has been made` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the order so far` IS A `The order so far`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no police order has been made` IF
    CONSIDER `the order so far`
    WHEN `no order has been made yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an interim order has been made` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a final order has been made` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police order has been made` THEN FALSE

-- The breach questions: a police order is a police order, whatever kind is named; otherwise the kind made. The kind is
-- read only after the police check, so for a police order it is not read.
GIVEN `the order so far` IS A `The order so far`
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order`
GIVETH A `Kind of order`
`the kind bound by` `the order so far` `the order made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the order so far`
    WHEN `no order has been made yet` THEN `the order made`
    WHEN `an interim order has been made` THEN `the order made`
    WHEN `a final order has been made` THEN `the order made`
    WHEN `a police order has been made` THEN `a police order`

-- s 7: a respondent "must be natural persons" -- the person asking is one. s 50: "No restraining order is to be made
-- against a child who is under 10 years of age." The baseline's rule reads both from `My case`; asked by the person
-- themselves, only the age is a fact to state. The age limit is the baseline's own number.
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an order can be made against a person of` `my age in years` IF
    `my age in years` AT LEAST `the youngest respondent`

-- s 32(2): "If a respondent does not return the respondent's endorsement copy of an interim order in accordance with
-- section 31, the interim order becomes a final order with the same terms as the interim order"; (3)(b): it comes into
-- force "at the end of the 21 day period referred to in section 31". Not in the baseline.
`s 32(2) -- an interim order not answered becomes final` MEANS TRUE

-- s 61(6): "A prosecution for an offence under subsection (1), (1A) or (2a) must be commenced within 2 years after the
-- day on which the offence is alleged to have been committed." Those are the FVRO, VRO and police order offences; the
-- MRO offence (s 61(2)) is not named, and its limit comes from outside this Act (baseline finding 12). Not in the
-- baseline.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of order`
GIVETH A `Time to prosecute`
`s 61(6) -- the time to prosecute a breach of` `the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `an FVRO` THEN `within years of the day of the breach` 2
    WHEN `a VRO` THEN `within years of the day of the breach` 2
    WHEN `an MRO` THEN `not set by this Act: s 61(6) does not cover a breach of an MRO`
    WHEN `a police order` THEN `within years of the day of the breach` 2

§§ `For the person who wants to be protected`

§§§ `ss 4, 5A, 6 -- the relationship and the violence`

@export Are the respondent and I in a family relationship (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how we are connected` IS A `The relationship between us` @desc How you and the respondent are, or were, connected
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Are the respondent and I in a family relationship` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Are we in a family relationship` `how we are connected`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has the respondent committed family violence against me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 5A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how we are connected` IS A `The relationship between us` @desc How you and the respondent are, or were, connected
      `what the respondent has done` IS A `What the respondent has done to me` @desc What the respondent has done or threatened
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has the respondent committed family violence against me, as I put it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Has the respondent committed family violence against me` `how we are connected` `what the respondent has done`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has the respondent committed personal violence against me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how we are connected` IS A `The relationship between us` @desc How you and the respondent are, or were, connected
      `what the respondent has done` IS A `What the respondent has done to me` @desc What the respondent has done or threatened
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has the respondent committed personal violence against me, as I put it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Has the respondent committed personal violence against me` `how we are connected` `what the respondent has done`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7, 10D, 11A, 12A, 34, 35A, 50 -- which order can protect me`

@export Can any restraining order be made against the respondent at all: are they an individual of 10 or over (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 7, 50)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your relationship to the respondent, what they did, what the court is satisfied of, and who they are
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can any restraining order be made against the respondent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Can an order be made against this respondent` `my case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a court make a family violence restraining order for me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 10D(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your relationship to the respondent, what they did, what the court is satisfied of, and who they are
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a court make a family violence restraining order for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Can a court make an FVRO for me` `my case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the court make the family violence restraining order for me, unless there are special circumstances (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 10D(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your relationship to the respondent, what they did, what the court is satisfied of, and who they are
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the court make the family violence restraining order for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Must the court make the FVRO` `my case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a court make a violence restraining order for me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 11A, 12A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your relationship to the respondent, what they did, what the court is satisfied of, and who they are
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a court make a violence restraining order for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Can a court make a VRO for me` `my case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a court make a misconduct restraining order for me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 34, 35A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your relationship to the respondent, what they did, what the court is satisfied of, and who they are
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a court make a misconduct restraining order for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Can a court make an MRO for me` `my case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Which restraining order can protect me, if any (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) Parts 1B, 2 and 3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your relationship to the respondent, what they did, what the court is satisfied of, and who they are
GIVETH A `Which order, if it arises`
`Which restraining order can protect me, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `the answer is` (`Which restraining order can protect me` `my case`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 24A, 25, 38 -- who may apply`

@export May this person apply for the order to protect me: me, a police officer, my parent or guardian, a child welfare officer, or my guardian (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 24A, 25, 38)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order I want` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The order you want
      `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant` @desc Who would make the application
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I have a guardian under the Guardianship and Administration Act 1990` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardian has been appointed for you under that Act
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May this person apply for the order to protect me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`May this person apply for me` `the order I want` `the applicant` `my age in years` `I have a guardian under the Guardianship and Administration Act 1990`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 16, 18, 20, 26, 29, 31, 39 -- interim orders`

@export Can I get a restraining order by telephone, without going to court (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 18, 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order I want` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The order you want
      `an authorised person applies for me or introduces me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a police officer (or other authorised person) makes the application or introduces you to the magistrate
      `the magistrate is satisfied it is urgent or impractical to apply in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the magistrate accepts that going to court in person is impractical or the order is urgent
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I get a restraining order by telephone` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Can I get a telephone order` `the order I want` `an authorised person applies for me or introduces me` `the magistrate is satisfied it is urgent or impractical to apply in person`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I ask for a first hearing without the respondent, to get an interim order (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 26, 29, 39)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order I want` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The order you want
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I get an interim order at a first hearing without the respondent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Can I get an interim order before the respondent is heard` `the order I want`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export At most how many months does an interim telephone order protect me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 16(4)(d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Months`
`At most how many months does a telephone order protect me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN months `How many months can a telephone order protect me at most`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days does the respondent have, after being served with my interim order, to return the endorsement copy and say whether they object (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 31)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
GIVETH A `Days`
`How many days does the respondent have to object to my interim order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN
        IF `no interim order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE days `How many days does the respondent have to object`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 30A, 30F -- police orders`

@export Can a police officer make an order on the spot to protect me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 30A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how we are connected` IS A `The relationship between us` @desc How you and the respondent are, or were, connected
      `the officer believes it is urgent or impractical to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer reasonably believes the s 20(1) urgency criteria are met
      `the officer believes family violence was committed and is likely again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer reasonably believes the respondent committed family violence and will do it again
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to apprehend family violence against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer has reasonable grounds to apprehend family violence will be committed against you
      `the officer believes an order is necessary for someone's safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer believes an order is necessary to ensure someone's safety
      `a telephone application on the same facts was dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a magistrate dismissed a telephone application about the same facts
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a police officer make an order on the spot to protect me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN `yes if` (`Can the police make an order to protect me now` `how we are connected` `the officer believes it is urgent or impractical to go to court` `the officer believes family violence was committed and is likely again` `the officer has reasonable grounds to apprehend family violence against me` `the officer believes an order is necessary for someone's safety` `a telephone application on the same facts was dismissed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export At most how many hours does a police order protect me, once it is served (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 30F(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Hours`
`At most how many hours does a police order protect me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN hours `How many hours can a police order protect me`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many hours must a police order be served on the respondent, or it lapses (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 30F(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Hours`
`Within how many hours must a police order protecting me be served` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN hours `Within how many hours must a police order be served`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 16A, 16B, 37, 50A -- how long a final order lasts`

@export How many months will the final order protect me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 16A, 16B, 37, 50A; an interim order the respondent does not object to becomes final, s 32)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
      `months specified in the order` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the order specifies, in months; 0 if it specifies none
      `the respondent is a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the respondent is under 18
GIVETH A `Months`
`How many months will the final order protect me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN
        IF `no interim or final order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE months (`How many months would the final order protect me` `the order made` `months specified in the order` `the respondent is a child`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 61, 61A, 61B -- if the respondent breaches the order`

@export What is the most the respondent can be fined for breaching my order (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 61)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the respondent can be fined for breaching my order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN
        IF `no order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is the most the respondent can be fined for a breach` (`the kind bound by` `the order so far` `the order made`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the longest the respondent can be imprisoned for breaching my order, in months (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 61; none for an MRO)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the longest the respondent can be imprisoned for breaching my order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN
        IF `no order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE months (`What is the longest imprisonment for a breach in months` (`the kind bound by` `the order so far` `the order made`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the respondent be imprisoned for breaching my order again, after two earlier breach convictions within 2 years (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 61A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
      `days the respondent committed breaches they were convicted of, in the 2 years before` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many different days, in the 2 years before this conviction, the respondent committed FVRO, VRO or police order breaches they were convicted of
      `the court finds the s 61A(6) exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that imprisonment would be clearly unjust and that the person bound is unlikely to be a threat to the safety of a person protected or the community (s 61A(6))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the respondent be imprisoned for breaching my order again` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN
        IF `no order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the respondent be locked up for a repeated breach` (`the kind bound by` `the order so far` `the order made`) `days the respondent committed breaches they were convicted of, in the 2 years before` `the court finds the s 61A(6) exception`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I commit an offence if I help the respondent breach my order (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 61B(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I commit an offence if I help the respondent breach my order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I want to be protected from someone` THEN
        IF `no order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `Do I commit an offence by aiding a breach of my order`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person an order is sought or made against (the respondent)`

§§§ `ss 7, 50 -- can an order be made against me at all`

@export Can a restraining order be made against me at all, given my age (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 7, 50)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a restraining order be made against me at all` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN `yes if` (`an order can be made against a person of` `my age in years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 31, 32 -- an interim order against me`

@export Within how many days of being served with the interim order must I return its endorsement copy to the registrar, saying whether I object to it becoming final (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 31)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days must I return the endorsement copy of the interim order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no interim order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE days `How many days does the respondent have to object`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I do not return the endorsement copy within those 21 days, does the interim order become a final order against me, in the same terms, at the end of them (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 32(2), (3)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`If I do not return the endorsement copy does the interim order become final` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no interim order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `s 32(2) -- an interim order not answered becomes final`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 16A, 16B, 37, 50A -- how long a final order binds me`

@export How many months will the final order bind me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) ss 16A, 16B, 37, 50A: at most 6 months if I was a child when it was made)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
      `months specified in the order` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the order specifies, in months; 0 if it specifies none
      `I was under 18 when the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a child (under 18) when the final order was made
GIVETH A `Months`
`How many months will the final order bind me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no interim or final order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE months (`How many months would the final order protect me` `the order made` `months specified in the order` `I was under 18 when the order was made`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 30F, 30H -- a police order against me`

@export For at most how many hours does the police order bind me, once it is served on me (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 30F(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
GIVETH A `Hours`
`For how many hours does the police order bind me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no police order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE hours `How many hours can a police order protect me`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many hours of being made must the police order be served on me, or it lapses (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 30F(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
GIVETH A `Hours`
`Within how many hours must the police order be served on me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no police order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE hours `Within how many hours must a police order be served`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 30H: "The duration of a police order cannot be extended or renewed and another police order cannot be made in
-- relation to the same facts."
@export Can the police extend or renew the police order against me, or make another one on the same facts (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 30H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the police extend or renew the police order against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no police order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE no
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 61, 61A -- if I breach the order`

@export What is the most I can be fined for breaching the order (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 61)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for breaching the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is the most the respondent can be fined for a breach` (`the kind bound by` `the order so far` `the order made`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for breaching the order, in months (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 61; none for an MRO)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned for breaching the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE months (`What is the longest imprisonment for a breach in months` (`the kind bound by` `the order so far` `the order made`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I am convicted of breaching the order again, after earlier breach convictions on two or more days within 2 years, must I be imprisoned (or, as a child, imprisoned or detained) (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 61A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
      `days I committed breaches I was convicted of, in the 2 years before` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many different days, in the 2 years before this conviction, you committed FVRO, VRO or police order breaches you were convicted of
      `the court finds the s 61A(6) exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that imprisonment would be clearly unjust and that the person bound is unlikely to be a threat to the safety of a person protected or the community (s 61A(6))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be imprisoned if I am convicted of breaching the order again` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the respondent be locked up for a repeated breach` (`the kind bound by` `the order so far` `the order made`) `days I committed breaches I was convicted of, in the 2 years before` `the court finds the s 61A(6) exception`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how long after a breach must a prosecution for it be started (Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) s 61(6): 2 years for an FVRO, VRO or police order; the Act sets none for an MRO)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the order so far` IS A `The order so far` @desc Whether an order has been made yet between you and the other person, and which: an interim order (made by telephone or at a first hearing without the respondent), a final order, or a police order made on the spot by a police officer
      `the order made` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The kind of order that was made: an FVRO, a VRO, an MRO or a police order
GIVETH A `Time to prosecute`
`Within how long must a prosecution for my breach be started` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me` THEN
        IF `no order has been made` `the order so far`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `s 61(6) -- the time to prosecute a breach of` (`the kind bound by` `the order so far` `the order made`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
